<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
    <key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key><true/>
    <key>NSPrincipalClass</key><string>NSApplication</string>
    <key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key><string>26.0</string>
    <!--
    System shell association reference. Uncomment and adapt for an archive/utility
    app; see Docs/shell-context-menu.md. These two blocks are not active in the
    generic template.

    Document types: appear in the file's "Open With" submenu.
    <key>CFBundleDocumentTypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>CFBundleTypeName</key><string>Archive</string>
            <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key><string>Viewer</string>
            <key>LSHandlerRank</key><string>Alternate</string>
            <key>LSItemContentTypes</key>
            <array>
                <string>public.zip-archive</string>
                <string>public.tar-archive</string>
                <string>org.gnu.gzip-archive</string>
            </array>
            <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
            <array>
                <string>zip</string><string>7z</string><string>rar</string>
                <string>tar</string><string>gz</string><string>tgz</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>

    Services: a Finder right-click "Services" entry. The service selector is
    dispatched to the open-documents inbox by cove-shell once the app registers
    a services provider. NSSendFileTypes is the file-service key; NSSendTypes is
    for pasteboard types and does not match Finder's file selection reliably.
    <key>NSServices</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSMenuItem</key><dict><key>default</key><string>Extract with this app</string></dict>
            <key>NSMessage</key><string>coveExtractService:</string>
            <key>NSSendFileTypes</key><array><string>public.item</string></array>
        </dict>
    </array>
    -->
</dict></plist>
